Internal decision infrastructure, not a business with customers.

Its own VENTURE.yaml records the hypothesis test (checked 2026-08-20): a
buyer, a price, and a route to one were checked in turn and none is present.
Access is a single-email Cloudflare Access whitelist for the owner, no
pricing or purchase surface exists anywhere in `src/`, and there is no
listing or distribution channel. Its own scoring data already said so:
`portfolio/scoring/venture-scores.yaml`'s `floor_note` scored it 2/10 on
time-to-revenue for exactly this reason before this marker existed.

Structurally, `src/lib/evaluation.ts` is the portfolio's own scoring engine
(`portfolio/scoring/venture-scores.yaml` records
`method: ventures/ai-first-markets/src/lib/evaluation.ts`, and roughly
seventeen files across the router, scoring, research, and pipeline reference
this path) and the app itself is the portfolio's private market-map tool, not
a product being sold. Counting it under `ventures/` drew $50/mo of protected
explore budget toward a directory `portfolio/router/allocate.py` could never
convert to revenue.

This marker makes that call machine-readable so `portfolio/router/allocate.py`,
`portfolio/scoring/score_ventures.py`, and `portfolio/router/validate.py` all
skip the directory consistently, per the marker-precedence fix in #334. Its
`portfolio/scoring/venture-scores.yaml` entry is deliberately kept: reclassified
is not removed, and `score_ventures.py --check` scores it (11 scored) while the
router allocates only the 10 unmarked ventures. A marked directory keeping its
score row is allowed by the `documented_slugs()` superset added in #341, so
`--check` passes with the row present rather than requiring it be deleted.

Whether this belongs under `ventures/` or `platform/` is still the open
structural question its own VENTURE.yaml flags — this marker does not settle
it, and deliberately stops short of the directory move (and the CI
path-filter, router, and doc updates that move would need) since the marker
alone is now sufficient to stop future budget misallocation. VENTURE.yaml is
left in place rather than deleted, matching the transitional state the
NOT-A-VENTURE + VENTURE.yaml coexistence is designed for.
